# frontend/.env - was committed since the very first commit, unlike
# ai-runtime/.gitignore and backend/.gitignore, which already correctly
# excluded their own .env files (same gap the root .env had - see the
# root .gitignore's own comment and its pairing commit). Untracking now
# stops a real deployment's local overrides (e.g. this project's GCP VM,
# which needs its own public IP here instead of localhost) from being
# silently reverted by every future `git pull` - see .env.example for the
# placeholder values a fresh checkout should use.
.env
